{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Behold, one people.</b> All this goodness they have with them — that they are one people, and one language for all of them — and this thing they have begun to do." "<b>They have begun.</b> Like אָמְרָם, עֲשׂוֹתָם — 'to do them': they have begun to do." "<b>Nothing will be withheld from them… to do.</b> With wonder. יִבָּצֵר is a term of withholding, as the Targum renders; and similar to it: ״יִבְצֹר רוּחַ נְגִידִים״ (Psalms 76)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:18.684192959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}